          "tz": 480
        },
        "subject": "LU-20758 tests: fix sanity/63c OST_SYNC upper bound",
        "message": "LU-20758 tests: fix sanity/63c OST_SYNC upper bound\n\nfix sanity/63c OST_SYNC RPC range from [stripes, 2*stripes)\nto [stripes, 2*stripes].\n\nsanity.sh test_63c writes a fully striped file and expects the\nOST_SYNC RPC count to be in the range [stripes, 2 * stripes),\nbut a valid run can reach exactly 2 * stripes\nwhen both close-triggered CL_FSYNC_ALL\nand background/reclaim CL_FSYNC_RECLAIM sync each stripe.\n\nThat legitimate upper bound is currently excluded by the strict\n`<` comparison, causing an off-by-one failure such as:\n\n  sanity test_63c: @@@@@@ FAIL: expect OST striped 3208 == 3192 + 8\n\nChange the upper bound from [stripes, 2*stripes) to\n[stripes, 2*stripes] will fix this error.\n\nFixes: 1cf465d79a3b (\"LU-16049 llite: add sync_on_close option\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity\nSigned-off-by: Xiyang Wang <xiwang@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I1bb2d62b858a27339a5b74270c143e6bc6bc19a2\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
